// Component: infra/docker.py -- paused indefinitely (decision-0001).
// oci-specific plumbing: `docker exec` stands in for a host pid and a
// supervisor program while oci is paused. Not part of rule 3's slice
// (that names only domain/jail_types and presentation/drivers) -- it is
// the paused paragraph's own bundle. bwrap already has its own infra
// primitive too (`processes`, modeled separately); Seatbelt likely will
// once built. Deliberately left out of views/brig/jail-types.c4, which
// shows only rule 3's two-file shape per type -- see that view's own
// comment for why.
model {
  extend brig.library {
    docker = component 'Docker' {
      #paused
      technology 'Python 3.15, stdlib only'
      description 'Would run and signal a container via `docker exec`, standing in for a host pid and a supervisor program. Plain data in and out -- never a brig type -- so only oci\'s driver knows what the data means. Paused indefinitely (decision-0001) -- it keeps its place in the layout but has no order of work yet.'
    }
  }
}
